Free the compiled pattern (and regexec()'s match array) before gsub()
and regexec() reject an invalid input string, so the grep, character and
parse targets stop reporting the compiled TRE/PCRE2 pattern as a leak.

do_gsub() and do_regexec() (src/main/grep.c) compile the pattern first
and validate each element of 'text' inside the loop over it; the error
"input string N is invalid in this locale" raised there unwinds past the
tre_regfree() / pcre2_code_free() / free(pmatch) at the end of the
function.  do_gsub()'s teardown moves into a helper that it also calls
before signalling; do_regexec() frees before its two errors.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5223944442150912 (libFuzzer_r_parse,
Direct-leak, tre_compile <- do_gsub: a gsub() call in R's own code).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #400, filed 2026-10-23 (no Bugzilla
report yet).  It supersedes PR #375, the version carried here, by running
the matching loops of grep(), regexpr(), gsub(), regexec() and strsplit()
under a cleanup context, which also covers options(warn = 2) turning the
first untranslatable-input warning into an error inside wtransChar2().
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/grep.c
+++ b/src/main/grep.c
@@ -2091,6 +2091,43 @@
  * either once or globally.
  * The functions are loosely patterned on the "sub" and "gsub" in "nawk". */
 
+/* Release whatever do_gsub() compiled.  Also called before an error is
+   signalled part-way through the text vector, since the unwind would
+   otherwise leak the compiled pattern. */
+static void gsub_free_pattern(bool fixed_opt, bool perl_opt, regex_t *reg,
+			      const unsigned char *tables,
+#ifdef HAVE_PCRE2
+			      pcre2_code *re, pcre2_match_data *mdata,
+			      pcre2_match_context *mcontext)
+#else
+			      pcre *re_pcre, pcre_extra *re_pe)
+#endif
+{
+    if (fixed_opt) ;
+    else if (perl_opt) {
+#ifdef HAVE_PCRE2
+	pcre2_match_data_free(mdata);
+	pcre2_code_free(re);
+	pcre2_match_context_free(mcontext);
+	if (tables)
+	    /* new PCRE2 will have pcre2_maketables_free() */
+	    free((void *)tables);
+#else
+	if (re_pe) pcre_free_study(re_pe);
+	pcre_free(re_pcre);
+	pcre_free((void *)tables);
+#endif
+    } else tre_regfree(reg);
+}
+
+#ifdef HAVE_PCRE2
+# define GSUB_FREE_PATTERN() \
+    gsub_free_pattern(fixed_opt, perl_opt, &reg, tables, re, mdata, mcontext)
+#else
+# define GSUB_FREE_PATTERN() \
+    gsub_free_pattern(fixed_opt, perl_opt, &reg, tables, re_pcre, re_pe)
+#endif
+
 attribute_hidden SEXP do_gsub(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 {
     SEXP pat, rep, text, ans;
@@ -2247,18 +2284,24 @@
